content.text:
## Investigation

The Java DSL encodes the UI tree as **varargs inside a method call**:

```java
VStack.make(...).children(
    Text.make(...),
    HStack.make(...).children(...)
)
```

That is the root cause of both complaints:

- IDEs fold **braces and lambda bodies**, not argument lists — so no per-subtree collapse.
- Auto-indent has no brace anchor, so children drift. `LayoutSection.java:44-59` already shows `Spacer.make()`, `Rectangle.make()`, `Divider.make()` at column 0.
- Deep trees force local variables (`playControl`, `trackInfo`, …) just to keep them readable.

Good news: `spec/DSL.md:137` already permits the child subtree to be a "vararg, macro, builder, or lambda". And every child funnels through `ViewBuilder.children(...)` → `setChildren(List<View>)` (`ViewBuilder.java:41`), so a block form can be **byte-identical** — no protocol or emitter change.

## Recommended improvement: block child scope

Add a tiny collector and an overload:

```java
@FunctionalInterface
public interface ChildScope {
    void add(View... children);
    default void addAll(Collection<? extends View> children) { ... }
}
```

```java
// ViewBuilder
public ViewBuilder<V, C> children(Consumer<ChildScope> content) { ... }
```

Plus static `children(Consumer<ChildScope>)` overloads on the content-bearing views (`VStack`, `HStack`, `ZStack`, `Grid`, `GridRow`, `ScrollView`, Lazy*, `Group`, `Button`, `Picker`, `Menu`).

Before (`LayoutSection.java:34-59`):

```java
.children(
        Grid.children(cell("1"), cell("2"), cell("3")),
        LazyVStack.make().modifiers(padding(4))
                .children(Text.make("A"), Text.make("B")),
Spacer.make().modifiers(),
Divider.make().modifiers());
```

After:

```java
.children(c -> {
    c.add(Grid.children(cell("1"), cell("2"), cell("3")));
    c.add(LazyVStack.make()
            .modifiers(padding(4))
            .children(rows -> {
                rows.add(Text.make("A"));
                rows.add(Text.make("B"));
            }));
    c.add(Spacer.make().modifiers());
    c.add(Divider.make().modifiers());
});
```

Now each container is a `{ ... }` block: IDEs fold it independently, indentation is brace-anchored, and the varargs form still works for small trees.

**Costs:** one `add` per child (slightly more verbose); nested lambdas can't reuse the same parameter name (`c -> { ... c -> ... }` is illegal), so use semantic names (`row`, `info`, `content`); migrating demos is a mechanical but large diff.

## Secondary polish

- Use one `.modifiers(...)` call per node instead of repeated `.modifiers(...)`.
- Keep leaves on one line; extract repeated subtrees into named views/helpers.
- Optional later: `make(config, content)` two-lambda sugar, or `c.text(...)`/`c.spacer()` shortcuts. Defer unless wanted.

## Alternatives considered

- **Compact `UI.vstack(...)` facade** — very readable, but a parallel surface to `make`/`children`; more churn and spec work.
- **Push/pop builder** (`.begin()`/`.end()`) — no lambda shadowing, but error-prone and not fluent.
- **Conventions only** — doesn't fix IDE folding.

## Proposed plan

1. Add `ChildScope` + `ViewBuilder` overload + static overloads on content-bearing views.
2. Tests: block vs varargs render-tree equality, order, nesting, modifiers-in-any-order; optionally frame-byte equality.
3. Update `spec/DSL.md` (§2 and the §9.3 language table) and `lib/java/pathland-view/status.md`.
4. Migrate demo views (`LayoutSection`, `PlayerControls`, `Sidebar`, `HomeView`, `MusicPlayerView`, `LibraryView`, …) — or a separate change.
5. Verify with `cd lib/java && mvn install`.

Locked: **Option 1 (block child scope)**, documented as an **optional alternative**, first change = **API + tests + spec only**.

## What the "Compact UI facade" would look like

A new `UI` namespace that wraps construction + children + leaf shortcuts, so a whole tree reads like markup:

```java
public final class UI {
    public static View vstack(Consumer<VStack.Config> values, Consumer<ChildScope> content)
    public static View hstack(Consumer<HStack.Config> values, Consumer<ChildScope> content)
    public static View zstack(Consumer<ZStack.Config> values, Consumer<ChildScope> content)

    public static View button(Consumer<Button.Config> values)
    public static View button(Consumer<Button.Config> values, Consumer<ChildScope> content)

    public static View text(String text)
    public static View text(Signal<String> text)
    public static View icon(IconName name)
    public static View spacer()
    public static View divider()
    // …one pair per view/control
}
```

Call site:

```java
return UI.vstack(v -> v.alignment(HorizontalAlignment.LEADING).spacing(8), page -> {
    page.add(UI.text("Pathland").modifiers(fontSize(18), FontWeight.BOLD));

    page.add(UI.hstack(h -> h.spacing(4), row -> {
        row.add(UI.button(b -> b.title("+").action(() -> count.update(n -> n + 1))));
        row.add(UI.button(b -> b.title("−").action(() -> count.update(n -> n - 1))));
        row.add(UI.button(b -> b.title("Reset").action(() -> count.set(0))));
    }));

    // A button with an icon child needs the two-lambda form:
    page.add(UI.button(b -> b.action(this::prev),
            label -> label.add(UI.icon(IconName.SKIP_BACK))));

    page.add(UI.text(computed(() -> "Count: " + count.get())));
    page.add(UI.spacer());
}).modifiers(padding(24));
```

This is the most "markup-like" option, but:

- It duplicates every factory (`UI.vstack` vs `VStack.make`, `UI.text` vs `Text.make`, …) — two places to keep in sync.
- It adds a second authoring surface to the spec/generation contract.
- Two lambdas per container get noisy, and nested lambdas still can't reuse a parameter name.
- Modifiers still chain outside the call, so the element still isn't fully self-contained.

A less duplicative middle ground would be a two-lambda `build` on the existing types:

```java
return VStack.build(v -> v.spacing(8), page -> {
    page.add(Text.make("Pathland").modifiers(fontSize(18), FontWeight.BOLD));
    page.add(HStack.build(h -> h.spacing(4), row -> {
        row.add(Button.make(b -> b.title("+").action(...)));
    }));
}).modifiers(padding(24));
```

Option 1 (`children(c -> …)`) gets nearly the same structural readability without a parallel namespace or duplicated leaf factories.

## Finalized plan (Option 1)

1. Add `ChildScope` (`add(View...)`, `addAll(Collection<? extends View>)`).
2. Add `ViewBuilder.children(Consumer<ChildScope>)`; static `children(Consumer<ChildScope>)` overloads on content-bearing views.
3. Tests: block vs varargs render-tree equality, order, nesting, modifiers-in-any-order; optionally frame-byte equality.
4. Document in `spec/DSL.md` as an **optional alternative** (varargs stays canonical); update `lib/java/pathland-view/status.md`.
5. No demo migration in this change; verify with `cd lib/java && mvn install`.

